{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>He binds.</b> The yod is added, like היושבי (Psalms 123:1), לסוסתי (Song of Songs 1:9)." "<b>His donkey.</b> Like עַל שְׁלֹשִׁים עִירִים (Judges 10:4)." "And the yod of בני אתונו is added, or the meaning is that אסרי governs itself and another." "<b>And to the choice vine.</b> Doubled, for it is like גפן, and עירון like אתון." "Likewise ובדם ענבים סותה. Some say it is like כסותו and it is lacking a kaf. What seems correct to me is that it is from the root מסוה (Exodus 34:33), and the meaning is that the yield of his vineyards multiplies until he unsaddles his donkey to the vine, and does not worry if it eats grapes, and under the grapevines he washes his garment in wine, and likens it to blood because it reddens. This is by way of parable, like יטפו הרים עסיס (Joel 4:18), until he is called חכלילי עינים from the abundance of wine that he drinks, for redness appears in the eye from wine intoxication, and his teeth are white from the abundance of eating fat."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:26.685922358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}